Falsifies `paging::nth_allocation::a_failed_map_span_maps_a_prefix`.

The defect: a "best effort" `map_span`. A leaf whose tables cannot be allocated is skipped, the
rest of the span is mapped, and the first error is returned at the end. The caller sees
`OutOfPageFrames` and unwinds what it believes is the mapped prefix, and the leaves past the gap stay
mapped with nobody recording them: a half-installed grant.

Expected to fail: assertion (2), "what is left mapped is not a prefix of the request", at
`map_span` with allocation 0 failed (the 4 KiB head is skipped and every block after it is mapped).

`script/falsifications --sweep paging` replays it, weekly and per pull request, since milestone
742 (every test is falsified as routine). By hand, the same thing is:

    git apply crates/paging/falsifications/nth_allocation.a_failed_map_span_maps_a_prefix.patch
    cargo test -p paging --test nth_allocation a_failed_map_span_maps_a_prefix        # must fail
    git apply -R crates/paging/falsifications/nth_allocation.a_failed_map_span_maps_a_prefix.patch

Run on 2026-10-04 (UTC), patagonia: red as predicted, green again after the revert.

